Z||000003||Gold-86SE||05-04-2000||06:04 PM||||<BR>I am making a big assumption here.<P>1) I am assuming that you have a 4cyl.<P>2) And if you do have a 4 cyl that you are refering to the metal tube that runs up from (attached to) the cat. converter.<P>This tube connects the cat. converter to the underside of the air intake (where your air cleaner is housed).<P>Examine the bottom of your air intake and you will see a circular extension which aims down toward the back of the engine (when the air intake is attached to the throttle body).  The metal tube running from the cat. attaches to this circular extension.<P>If this is what you are talking about, then this tube is used during cold starts to feed the engine warm air, because the exhaust heats up faster than the engine itself.<BR>||||reg||3
